{"id": "EUVD-2026-86117", "enisaUuid": "b425de1c-b37b-34d6-9de7-d00ad0120d5a", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndrm/xe: Fix null pointer dereference in devcoredump cleanup\n\nIn xe_devcoredump_snapshot_free(), ss->gt may be NULL when the snapshot\nwas never fully populated (e.g., when cleanup is triggered without a\nprior capture). Guard the xe_guc_capture_put_matched_nodes() call with\nIS_ERR_OR_NULL() to prevent a null dereference.\n\nIn xe_devcoredump_free(), the deferred work is only queued when a\ncoredump is captured, so guard cancel_work_sync() with a check on\ncoredump->captured.", "datePublished": "2026-09-24T16:05:19", "dateUpdated": "2026-09-28T05:30:56", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f5c3144f783f91d74b4fae84fb8bd7a4edf001f8", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/12ef528d78adc8ea4e7e3db594f3bcac327e79fa"], "aliases": ["GHSA-847m-qmx9-284v", "CVE-2026-97519"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.15, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "1be48731-f89c-347e-a4e1-8952860f7fcb", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "ecb6336463911d6eb684998754f8701d0f437f18 <f5c3144f783f91d74b4fae84fb8bd7a4edf001f8"}, {"id": "248b1319-685d-38d9-8cf1-ddd72fb8a8c0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "ecb6336463911d6eb684998754f8701d0f437f18 <12ef528d78adc8ea4e7e3db594f3bcac327e79fa"}, {"id": "2cc9e355-150e-3ab2-902c-1c27d6085ecd", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2"}, {"id": "70fd5895-2711-3a89-b884-aeb96178a388", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "966e4b7a-1a6b-3e9d-abfb-b3ecbf55018d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.13"}, {"id": "d9f01416-9376-347f-8972-63b8a77867a5", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.53"